# Code Checks
{{#workflow}}
Requested Guide URI: `guide://_check`.
{{/workflow}}

## Directives

{{#workflow}}- Read `{{workflow-file}}` to identify the current issue and implementation scope.
- Update `{{workflow-file}}` to `phase: check` when changing phase, then send the complete file using `send_file_content`.
{{/workflow}}- Run the repository's required code validation commands.
- Fix failures that are in scope for the current issue.
- Record check results and remaining risks in `{{path.documents}}/` when useful.
- Keep handoff context `{{path.documents}}/context.json` updated at meaningful milestones when present.

## Guardrails

- Do not broaden implementation while checking; fix only issues required to make the current change correct.
- Treat every failure after work begins as related to the current change. The task starts from a passing main branch, so an untouched or unread test is not evidence that its failure is unrelated.
- Investigate direct and indirect effects of the current change before concluding that any failure has another cause.
- Do not skip tests or verification silently.
{{#openspec}}
## OpenSpec Association

Use `openspec-verify-change` during check phase to validate that implementation matches the OpenSpec artefacts. Use `openspec-sync-specs` only when main specs intentionally need updating outside archival. Keep `openspec-archive-change` for completed changes after verification and when the user or project process allows archiving.
{{/openspec}}
